# Testing Standards

Unless explicitly requested otherwise, all generated or modified .NET tests MUST follow these standards.

## Required

- Use **xUnit v3** (`xunit.v3` package) for all automated tests
- Use **NSubstitute** for mocks, stubs, and test doubles
- Use built-in **xUnit `Assert` methods** only
- Keep test dependencies to a minimum

## Prohibited

Do not introduce:

- FluentAssertions
- AwesomeAssertions
- Shouldly
- Moq
- NUnit
- MSTest

## Conventions

- Test projects require `<OutputType>Exe</OutputType>` (set in `tests/Directory.Build.props`)
- Use `[Trait("Category", "...")]` for filterable test categories
- Test method names may use `Method_When_Then` underscore convention (CA1707 suppressed in `tests/**/*.cs`)
- Hand-rolled fakes (e.g. `HttpMessageHandler`, `WebApplicationFactory`) are acceptable when more appropriate than NSubstitute

## Allowed supporting packages

- `bunit` — Blazor component tests
- `coverlet.collector` — code coverage
- `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing` — integration tests
- `Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk` + `xunit.runner.visualstudio` — VSTest runner
